WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.710
An agent nearly sent a message to

2
00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:04.130
every parent in my class.

3
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.260
It said the school trip was cancelled.

4
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.000
It wasn’t!

5
00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.450
Luckily, it asked me first.

6
00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:16.810
Today: why an agent must ask before it

7
00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:19.670
acts, and how to check in code.

8
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.320
Some things an agent does only read: the

9
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:27.420
weather, a timetable, a library search.

10
00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.700
Others change the world: sending a

11
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:33.820
message, booking, paying, deleting.

12
00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:36.190
Reading can’t do much harm.

13
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.960
Acting can, and you can’t always undo it.

14
00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:43.330
So apps give each action a

15
00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:44.090
permission level.

16
00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:47.740
Read only: it may look, but not act.

17
00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:51.110
Ask first: it must show you the

18
00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:52.890
action and wait for your yes.

19
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.700
Allowed: it may act alone,

20
00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:58.100
for small, safe things.

21
00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:01.190
Here’s Darsi Tiny with a

22
00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:02.550
message for Mrs Mensah.

23
00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.550
It doesn’t send it straight away.

24
00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:07.000
It shows you the exact message

25
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.360
and asks for a yes or a no.

26
00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:12.330
Only after a yes does it call

27
00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:13.890
the send message tool.

28
00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:17.790
But asking first is learned, and

29
00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:19.290
learned behaviour can fail.

30
00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:22.780
Type only “Yes, send it” in

31
00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:24.860
Arabic, with nothing before it.

32
00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.660
Darsi Tiny makes up a message and tries to

33
00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:30.960
send it, though nobody was asked.

34
00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:32.630
Quick check!

35
00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:35.210
Darsi Tiny asked to send a

36
00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:36.650
message, and you replied.

37
00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:38.810
Where should the app check

38
00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:40.390
that you really said yes?

39
00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:44.590
In the app’s code, before the tool runs.

40
00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:47.280
Code doesn’t forget, and

41
00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.600
isn’t fooled by wording.

42
00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:51.500
If no one was asked, the app

43
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:52.460
blocks the message.

44
00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:55.110
And it keeps a record of what was sent.

45
00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:57.550
Here’s the check in Python.

46
00:01:58.350 --> 00:01:59.790
The app reads your reply.

47
00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:03.640
Only if it is exactly yes does it send.

48
00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.090
Anything else, even a

49
00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:08.390
maybe, means not sent.

50
00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:11.380
Some things an agent should

51
00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:13.540
never do, even with a yes.

52
00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:16.410
Never give it your password, or

53
00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:17.490
let it into your accounts.

54
00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:19.610
Never let it share a

55
00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:20.970
friend’s private details.

56
00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:22.900
And never let it send

57
00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:24.220
something you haven’t read.

58
00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:28.450
In the app, choose Ask first and

59
00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:31.690
message Mrs Mensah: say no, then yes.

60
00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:35.110
Then turn the code check off, choose

61
00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:38.390
Allowed, and send “Yes, send it” alone.

62
00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:41.420
Turn the check on again, and it’s blocked.

63
00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:43.320
Your turn.

64
00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.410
A study app’s agent wants to post your

65
00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:48.010
homework photo to the class group.

66
00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:49.490
What should you do first?

67
00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.480
Read exactly what it will

68
00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.620
post, then decide.

69
00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.200
Remember: reading is low risk,

70
00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:59.740
but acting needs your yes.

71
00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:03.010
A model’s asking can fail, so

72
00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:04.370
the app checks in code.

73
00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:06.710
And some things are never allowed.

74
00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:10.060
Try it yourself: open the settings

75
00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:11.700
of one app on your phone.

76
00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:14.810
Find one thing it may do without asking,

77
00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:17.530
such as posting or using your location.

78
00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:21.030
Switch it to ask first, or off.
